# Lantern: eight biome floor selection studies, part 1 of 2

This self-contained part contains: Woodland, Meadow, Bog, Rocky Highland.
Final comparison order: 1 Woodland, 2 Meadow, 3 Bog, 4 Rocky Highland, 5 Snow, 6 Arid Badlands, 7 Graveyard, 8 Crypt.
The water-free Bog replaces the superseded Marsh. Marsh and all rejected drafts are excluded. Use the eight-sample comparison; the earlier six-sample collection is superseded.

These are options for choosing favorites before any large-scene expansion, not approved production art. Floors are untouched native 1536×1024 PNGs, with no upscaling. No 8K output, engine/projection validation, or seamless-tiling proof is included or claimed.

## Contents and reproduction
- floors/: selected native floors for this part.
- prompts/: exact submitted selected prompts. Woodland/meadow use fresh retry 2; rejected first attempts are excluded.
- LOCKED_STYLE_VERBATIM.txt: exact locked style, verified verbatim in all prompts.
- references/: original approved hero and v04 hero/floor style-scale reference supplied to generation.
- metadata/: original per-biome metadata, source hashes, context hashes and portable composite settings.
- reproduce_contexts.py: relative-path Pillow compositing. Run `python reproduce_contexts.py` from any working directory (Python 3 and Pillow required). Output goes to reproduced_contexts/, or pass `--output PATH`.

The hero is not regenerated: crop original alpha at >30, resize with Lanczos to 68×160 pixels (160px visible-height convention), add the original small blurred ellipse shadow, and alpha-composite at recorded placement. Final context PNGs are delivered separately and omitted here for compact archives. Reproduction was verified pixel-identical against every final context. Original metadata/prompts are preserved verbatim, including historical absolute source paths. Portable mapping: floor basenames in floors/, exact prompts in prompts/, referenced PNG basenames in references/. The script uses bundled relative paths only.

## Limitations
Residual painterly mottling, gradients, noisy edges and oversized turf/stone details remain versus the strict flat-tone style. Woodland/meadow retries reduce these issues; highland is busier. Arid Badlands includes raised shale shelves: it is a terrain-relief concept, not a strictly flat floor. Selection-stage caveats also apply to graveyard and crypt; these are not proof of perfect style-lock compliance.

Camera 35.264° elevation / 45° azimuth is requested art direction, not verified geometry. Sunburst/model text is retained in the exact style/prompt; the built-in tool exposed no actual-model identifier, so actual model is unverified. Original hero/v04 image were style/scale conditioning references; floors are new compositions. No diagram/triangle guide was used.

SHA256SUMS.txt verifies every included payload file. Source provenance preserves copied source hashes. ZIP CRC verified during packaging. Native/context images were not modified; only the separate comparison sheet is scaled for viewing.
